Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: name the deb packages after the branch and local version

The build system picks up the kernel packages by name: it looks for
linux-image-<branch><localversion>, linux-headers-<branch><localversion> and
linux-dtb-<branch><localversion>, and derives them from BRANCH and
LOCALVERSION, both of which it passes on the make command line.

Upstream names them after the kernel release instead, so a mainline kernel
produces linux-image-7.2.0-sun50iw9 and the build system never finds it:

  [ error ] Installation of /root/linux-image-mainline-sun50iw9_1.0.4_arm64.deb
            failed

Follow the BRANCH/LOCALVERSION scheme when both are provided and keep the
upstream behaviour otherwise (e.g. for a plain "make bindeb-pkg").

diff --git a/scripts/package/mkdebian b/scripts/package/mkdebian
index d4b007b38..31690f691 100755
--- a/scripts/package/mkdebian
+++ b/scripts/package/mkdebian
@@ -169,7 +169,15 @@ sourcename=${KDEB_SOURCENAME:-linux-upstream}
 if [ "$ARCH" = "um" ] ; then
 	packagename=user-mode-linux
 else
-	packagename=linux-image
+	# Name the packages the way the build system expects them
+	# (linux-image-<branch><localversion>). Fall back to the kernel release
+	# when BRANCH/LOCALVERSION are not provided, as with a plain make.
+	if [ -n "${BRANCH:-}${LOCALVERSION:-}" ]; then
+		package_suffix="${BRANCH:-}${LOCALVERSION:-}"
+	else
+		package_suffix="${KERNELRELEASE}"
+	fi
+	packagename=linux-image-${package_suffix}
 fi
 
 debarch=
@@ -215,7 +223,7 @@ Build-Depends-Arch: bc, bison, flex,
  python3:native, rsync
 Homepage: https://www.kernel.org/
 
-Package: $packagename-${KERNELRELEASE}
+Package: $packagename
 Architecture: $debarch
 Description: Linux kernel, version ${KERNELRELEASE}
  This package contains the Linux kernel, modules and corresponding other
@@ -238,7 +246,7 @@ EOF
 if is_enabled CONFIG_MODULES; then
 cat <<EOF >> debian/control
 
-Package: linux-headers-${KERNELRELEASE}
+Package: linux-headers-${package_suffix}
 Architecture: $debarch
 Build-Profiles: <!pkg.${sourcename}.nokernelheaders>
 Description: Linux kernel headers for ${KERNELRELEASE} on $debarch
@@ -252,7 +260,7 @@ fi
 if is_enabled CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO; then
 cat <<EOF >> debian/control
 
-Package: linux-image-${KERNELRELEASE}-dbg
+Package: linux-image-${package_suffix}-dbg
 Section: debug
 Architecture: $debarch
 Build-Profiles: <!pkg.${sourcename}.nokerneldbg>
